WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.468
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.437
We're about to play a game
of "Box of Lies,"

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.504
but I'm gonna need some help.

00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:07.774
So joining me now
is one of the stars

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:10.243
of the new James Bond movie
"No Time to Die,"

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.078
which opens in theaters today.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.447
Please welcome Ana de Armas!

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.549
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.584
Very happy.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.319
Now, here's how it works.

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.354
We have nine mystery boxes

00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:24.690
containing objects
no one has ever seen before.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.293
On your turn, you pick a box,
take out an object,

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.695
and describe it
to your opponent.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.796
Then they have to guess

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.497
if you're lying
or telling the truth.

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:32.999
We'll play three rounds.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.367
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.070
[ Deep voice ] Ana, why don't
you pick the first box?

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.137
-Of course.

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:39.271
-Number 5!
-Oh.

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:40.739
-8!
-5!

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:42.909
[ Audience shouting ]

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.077
-I can't hear anything.
-No, you can't hear.

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:46.278
Now they're yelling
every number.

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:47.913
Yeah, they're just...

00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:51.984
[ Audience shouting ]

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:53.853
Yeah. They li-- 5's a --

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.922
Okay. Oh, this could be acting
right now.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:56.956
I don't know if it's heavy.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.324
-Doing this with heels
is not good.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.926
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.861
-Alright. Now, you open it,
and then you place it out here

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.295
so that the audience can see.

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:06.532
And the lying begins now --
or the truth telling begins now.

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:10.637
Here's where the game becomes...
-Okay.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.504
-...exciting.
-Okay.

00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:14.974
[ Light laughter ]
What?

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:18.544
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:20.280
This is very creepy.
Don't look.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.380
[ Laughter ]
-I'm not looking.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.650
I can't see it.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.885
-Who thinks of these things?

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.653
-Wha-- Who thinks --
are you asking --

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:30.122
Yeah. Okay.
-What to put in these boxes?

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:31.124
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.158
-All right.
Describe, describe.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.360
-Wow.
-What?

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.597
What is in --
What is in box number 5?

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:41.801
-Oh, my gosh.
So...this is a --

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.269
-You're lying.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.706
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:47.807
Oh, wait.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.209
-The -- So maybe
I don't know how to say

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:52.145
something in English, so...
-Okay.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.245
-You know.
-Okay.

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:54.813
-Is it "pumpkin"?

00:01:54.813 --> 00:01:56.683
-Okay, that sounds about right.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.184
Topical.
-Okay.

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:05.023
With three people taking --
it's like a Jacuzzi pumpkin.

00:02:05.023 --> 00:02:09.628
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:11.196
-I just want to hear you say
"Jacuzzi pumpkin,"

00:02:11.196 --> 00:02:12.531
like, forever, like...

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:13.933
"This is Jacuzzi pumpkin."

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.101
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.568
[ Both laugh ]
-Okay.

00:02:16.568 --> 00:02:17.670
-Gonna get better.
-Alright.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.839
So, is there three people
in the pumpkin?

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:23.109
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:24.777
♪♪

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:25.811
What?

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:27.513
-Ah! In the Jacuzzi.

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:29.115
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.850
-Uh-huh.
-Okay.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.352
One is...

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.354
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:36.689
I really don't know
who these people are, but...

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.657
[ Laughter ]
-You should know them.

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:40.026
-They're -- They're...

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:41.794
[ Both chuckle ]

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.363
...murderers.

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:44.630
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.232
They're, like, bad people.
-Oh, oh.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.466
-This is bad people.
-Okay.

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:49.635
These are three murderers
in a pumpkin hot tub.

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:51.971
[ Laughter ]
Now, if this is a lie,

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.606
then I will give you
a million dollars.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.208
There's no way you can be
making this up.

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:58.644
-Wait.
-I'm gonna say -- There's more?

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:00.980
-Smells good.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.948
-Okay.
I'm going to say...

00:03:02.948 --> 00:03:05.184
Ana de Armas...

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:07.386
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:09.222
...you are telling the truth.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.690
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.857
[ Clears throat ]

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:13.058
-You sure?

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:14.293
[ Light laughter ]
-Yes.

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:17.229
-God damn it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:18.898
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Did I -- Let me see it.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.299
[ Bell dings ]
-Who are these guys?

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:22.201
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, yeah. You don't know them?

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:24.303
Oh, no, that's -- that's...

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:25.637
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:25.637 --> 00:03:28.908
Yeah, that's from "Halloween."
That is Jar Jar Binks.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.576
-This is "Friday the 13th,"
isn't it?

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:31.677
-That's "Friday the 13th."
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:31.677 --> 00:03:33.179
-I don't know what that is.
-Yeah.

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:34.713
I don't know why he's --
he's drinking in a Jacu--

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:35.914
[ Light laughter ]
-Looks like a shrimp to me.

00:03:35.914 --> 00:03:36.982
-No, that's not a shrimp.

00:03:36.982 --> 00:03:38.383
It's -- It's from
a "Star Wars" movie.

00:03:38.383 --> 00:03:39.886
-Oh.
-A shrimp.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.187
It's Jar Jar -- Oh, yeah.
-I don't know.

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:42.288
-Good. Alright. Here.
You can put that right here.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.322
-Okay.
-Alright.

00:03:43.322 --> 00:03:44.690
Which number shall I...?

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:45.959
-3!
[ Audience shouting ]

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:48.160
-I heard a 3.
I heard a confident 3.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.295
And here we go.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.697
[ Grunting ]

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.666
-You're so bad.
-Thank you.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.369
[ Laughter ]
It's so heavy. Oh, my gosh.

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:58.537
[ Both chuckle ]
♪ La, la-la, la-la ♪

00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:02.041
[ Vocalizing ]

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.342
[ Humming ]

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:05.044
-It's very tempting.
Like, I want to...

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:06.412
-Yeah, I --

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:09.916
♪♪

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:11.917
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.917 --> 00:04:18.691
♪♪

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.926
I get it.
I get it.

00:04:20.926 --> 00:04:24.964
It's a lot -- It's --
It's a box inside of a box.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:29.234
And in there is a --
it's a bunch of butter knives

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:31.137
with a cable-knit sweater
over --

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:33.272
a tiny sweater over it.

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:35.040
I'm assuming this is
a Chris Evans reference.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.308
[ Laughter ]
And it's --

00:04:36.308 --> 00:04:40.179
a sweater over a bunch
of knives, butter knives.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.948
♪♪

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:45.218
-What? No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:46.485
-I wish I could --

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:48.687
-So, that's a Chris Evans
reference,

00:04:48.687 --> 00:04:50.823
and you just went
and picked that one out?

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:51.857
That's very strange.

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:53.325
So, you knew
that that was there.

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:56.062
-Well, we knew that you were
gonna be on the show, so, yeah.

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.729
♪♪

00:04:57.729 --> 00:05:00.299
You're in "Knives Out."
-No, I remember that.

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:03.769
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:05.938
So they probably thought
that that you would get it,

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:06.939
I'm assuming.

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.340
And then you would
have to laugh

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:12.478
and think of your memories
from being with Chris on set.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.980
-I think you're also telling
the truth,

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.116
because you just said it,
like, very fast.

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:19.451
And, like...
-I wish it was funnier.

00:05:19.451 --> 00:05:21.721
-Yeah, it's not that funny.
-No, it's pretty serious.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.256
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:24.657
-Yeah.
-Think I'm telling the truth?

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:25.991
-Telling the truth.

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:27.459
-I'm lying.
-No, you're not!

00:05:27.459 --> 00:05:29.995
-Yes. It's a "Marriage Story"
lunch box.

00:05:29.995 --> 00:05:31.197
-Oh, my God.
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:32.264
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Spinning Adam Dri--

00:05:32.264 --> 00:05:34.867
[ Laughter ]
They're arguing.

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:36.002
-God damn it! Okay.

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.569
-Scarlett Johansson
and Adam Driver

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:39.238
are arguing with each other,
spinning around --

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:40.539
-I can see. Yeah.
-It's a music box.

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:41.708
Thank you. Hey.

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:43.175
That was some good acting,
I thought.

00:05:43.175 --> 00:05:44.543
-That was so fast.
-That was quick thinking.

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:46.078
I thought -- Yeah, thank you.
I know.

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:48.247
Alright, here we go.
This one's for all the marbles.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:50.382
Ana, this one's
for 10,000 points.

00:05:50.382 --> 00:05:53.051
[ Audience shouting ]

00:05:53.051 --> 00:05:57.456
[ Shouting continues ]

00:05:57.456 --> 00:05:58.890
Oh.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.359
Controversial choice.

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:01.928
I would have went with 7,
myself.

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:03.962
-This one's very light.
Very light.

00:06:03.962 --> 00:06:05.664
-Oh, okay, very light.

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:06.865
Why would you do that?

00:06:06.865 --> 00:06:08.133
Oh, maybe --
-Just to show you.

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:10.303
-Yeah.
But maybe you're -- No?

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:13.205
-I don't know.
-Okay, I don't know either.

00:06:13.205 --> 00:06:14.973
It's very tricky.

00:06:14.973 --> 00:06:16.175
-Why is this...

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:18.911
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:21.380
What is this?

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.516
-If it's another pumpkin
with murderers in it...

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:24.883
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.883 --> 00:06:26.786
-No, it's -- it's --

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:29.388
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:32.124
♪♪

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:34.193
-I don't --
You're making a fa--

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.427
I have no idea what it is.
You're --

00:06:35.427 --> 00:06:38.531
-Well, trust me,
this is very strange.

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:40.132
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:43.569
♪♪

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.338
-Ana, just take a breath...

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:47.306
-Okay.
-...and describe what you see.

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.141
♪♪

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:51.543
-Okay. So...

00:06:51.543 --> 00:06:53.612
-[ Chuckles ]

00:06:53.612 --> 00:06:55.581
-It's a turtle.

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:56.849
"Turtle"?
-Yeah.

00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:57.917
-Okay.
-Turtle.

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.451
-Did I -- Turtle.

00:06:59.451 --> 00:07:02.387
-Tur-- Tur-- Turtle.
-Tur-- Turtle.

00:07:02.387 --> 00:07:04.390
-Turtle --
Oh, it's a turtle, okay.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:05.557
[ Laughter ]

00:07:05.557 --> 00:07:07.994
-Yeah, but instead of a...

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.295
-Shell?
-...shell...

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:11.496
-Uh-huh.
-...it's a hamburger.

00:07:11.496 --> 00:07:13.932
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:13.932 --> 00:07:16.135
Like, they dressed the --

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:18.871
The -- The turtle lives
in the burger.

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:21.173
[ Laughter ]

00:07:21.173 --> 00:07:23.342
♪♪

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:26.211
-"The turtle lives
in the burger" is so great.

00:07:26.211 --> 00:07:29.514
-It would be a turtle burger.
-It's a turtle burger.

00:07:29.514 --> 00:07:30.716
The turtle lives in the burger.

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:32.084
It's almost like
an acting exercise.

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.285
-It's on top of --

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:34.787
-"The turtle lives in
the burger. The turtle --

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:36.755
Okay, and let's yell, 'Action.'"
-Yeah.

00:07:36.755 --> 00:07:39.991
-So, it's a turtle
inside of a burger.

00:07:39.991 --> 00:07:41.259
-The shell is the burger.

00:07:41.259 --> 00:07:43.396
-The shell is a burger.
-Yeah.

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:46.665
-That sounds like something
our props department would do.

00:07:46.665 --> 00:07:50.536
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:07:50.536 --> 00:07:52.338
-But I'm not smelling
any hamburger.

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:53.672
[ Light laughter ]

00:07:53.672 --> 00:07:55.374
And I got to use all
my senses here, with this game.

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:56.909
-You didn't smell the Jacuzzi,
either.

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.945
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.945 --> 00:08:00.646
[ Laughing ]
That's true that I did not...

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:05.818
♪♪

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:07.820
-Ah. Ah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:09.187
-That might have been
a little give there.

00:08:09.187 --> 00:08:12.023
You were like...
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:12.023 --> 00:08:16.462
Why would you do that
if you were telling the truth?

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:19.065
Which means...
[ Both laugh ]

00:08:19.065 --> 00:08:21.400
...Ana de Armas...

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.035
you lie!

00:08:23.035 --> 00:08:25.437
[ Laughter ]
Let me see.

00:08:25.437 --> 00:08:26.839
-Oh, come on! This is --

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:29.241
-Oh, my gosh! I did it again?!
[ Bell dinging ]

00:08:29.241 --> 00:08:31.110
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Both laugh ]

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.378
Finally, I did really good.
Wow!

00:08:33.378 --> 00:08:34.747
-What is that?
-That was a good --

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:36.281
Turtle burger was good!

00:08:36.281 --> 00:08:37.449
I like turtle burger.

00:08:37.449 --> 00:08:38.584
We're going to put that
in the next game,

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:40.385
by the way, in honor of you!
-Thanks.

00:08:40.385 --> 00:08:41.721
-Ana de Armas, everybody!

